{"key":"ics/T1693.001","id":"T1693.001","name":"System Firmware","domain":"ics","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1693","tactics":["impair-process-control","inhibit-response-function","persistence"],"platforms":[],"environments":["ics-ot"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"System firmware on modern assets is often designed with an update feature. Older device firmware may be factory installed and require special reprograming equipment. When available, the firmware update feature enables vendors to remotely patch bugs and perform upgrades. Device firmware updates are often delegated to the user and may be done using a software update package. It may also be possible to perform this task over the network. An…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1693/001","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--68a9324d-a524-4766-a899-a026f68a33df","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.639Z","source_object_version":"1.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0038","name":"Application Log Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0038","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9c2fa0ae-7abc-485a-97f6-699e3b6cf9fa","page":"telemetry/DC0038/"},{"id":"DC0108","name":"Device Alarm","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0108","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9d56be63-3501-4dd3-bb5f-63c580833298","page":"telemetry/DC0108/"},{"id":"DC0004","name":"Firmware Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0004","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--b9d031bb-d150-4fc6-8025-688201bf3ffd","page":"telemetry/DC0004/"},{"id":"DC0085","name":"Network Traffic Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0085","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3772e279-27d6-477a-9fe3-c6beb363594c","page":"telemetry/DC0085/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0731","name":"Detection of System Firmware","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0731","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--09f46edf-33f9-4c23-af2f-74864c27f616","relationship_id":"relationship--c9efe378-d028-4c09-83c7-491fadc3a1f9"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN1864","name":"Analytic 1864","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0731#AN1864","guidance":"Monitor for firmware changes which may be observable via operational alarms from devices. Monitor device application logs for firmware changes, although not all devices will produce such logs. Monitor firmware for unexpected changes. Asset management systems should be consulted to understand known-good firmware versions. Dump and inspect BIOS images on vulnerable systems and compare against known good images. Analyze differences to determine if malicious changes have occurred. Log attempts to read/write to BIOS and compare against known patching behavior. Likewise, EFI modules can be collected and compared against a known-clean list of EFI executable binaries to detect potentially malicious…","platforms":["None"],"strategy_id":"DET0731"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0108","component":"Device Alarm","name":"Operational Databases","channel":"None","platforms":["None"],"analytic_id":"AN1864","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0731#AN1864","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0108/"},{"component_id":"DC0038","component":"Application Log Content","name":"Application Log","channel":"None","platforms":["None"],"analytic_id":"AN1864","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0731#AN1864","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0038/"},{"component_id":"DC0004","component":"Firmware Modification","name":"Firmware","channel":"None","platforms":["None"],"analytic_id":"AN1864","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0731#AN1864","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0004/"},{"component_id":"DC0085","component":"Network Traffic Content","n